ke that but  it's mostly all about the roofs which  you'll see in a second though aside from  that though it is a pretty simple  building and there's not really anything  special about it if this were an  alternate universe and we could have man  houses I would have loved to actually  put a man house in this building that's  also why I eventually ended up placing a  pretty large sort of backstage building  behind this the idea is that even though  this is a rather is small facade with a  like small wooden boardwalk next to it  it still has quite a lot of space behind  it for a potential like dark ride flat  ride at least and I would really figure  a Japanese mad house would have been  really awesome it's not on the game no  maybe that's a wink-wink nudge-nudge but  i don't think a japanese mad house is  the best thing to start recommending i  wouldn't exactly recommend it for the  game just wishful thinking and some who  would have loved to fit in here anyway  that is just majorly off-topic aside  from that no it has a pretty standard  sort of layouts with the oh my god I  completely forgot the name but like the  wooden thing along this site there where  you can sort of walk around with the  roof over the little wooden boardwalk  it's a little bit elevated as well and a  pretty simple sort of main part of the  building which is a bit higher than the  rest and has the actual curved roof  which turned out to be a little bit  harder to recreate than the other curved  roofs in the rest of the park and  especially a lot harder to do than just  the flat roofs because it doesn't just  involve slapping the the sandstone  pieces onto a curved roof because I  didn't quite want to have this exact  curved roof shape that the game gives  you I didn't want to get something a  little bit more smooth and more gentle  over curve so it eventually did end up  taking quite some time to get this  exactly right I did also catch the  interesting suggestion to try and  actually make the very typical Japanese  black sort of tiled roofs by using small  rocks and sinking them into the roof to  get that sort of dark black texture  going which I would have loved to do but  testing it it doesn't actually work  really well because the rocks are quite  large and you can't really hide them  under anything and it gets hard to  recreate the shape and it would have  also probably worked towards the lag in  this park already which I do have to say  one of the reasons also why I am ending  this bike and I've said this before but  at the moment is when I'm actually  really suffering the consequences I my  computer just can't really handle the  park anymore and I'm sort of on a steady  8 FPS but there's a tremendous amount of  click lag and UI is really slow as well  hence also why these time lapses are  still recorded at 12 times the speed but  especially in the next episode might be  a little bit slower than earlier  episodes just because it took longer to  do certain things and my computer really  can't handle much more of the park  anymore so yeah that's another one of  the reasons why I really couldn't finish  the park anymore though it was mainly  just a learning experience and I'm  really happy with how the parts are not  so far it's just one of the reasons why  I can't really go any further than what  I'm doing at the moment really anyway  that's the curved roof over there which  is I think just the best shaped roof at  least in the Japanese area which I have  so far it is kind of annoying to line  them all up and it is quite  time-consuming to do it in the exact way  which you want to but if anything it my  actually show of how incredibly flexible  this system already is and one of the  reasons why I'm also really looking  forward to the second alpha is for the  more free rotation that I mentioned  earlier in the video which might ruin  grizzly Valley but it's definitely an  amazing addition to the game because in  the future we won't really have to worry  about these different groups anymore to  get things to have specific rotations  because there will be three axis  rotation which is probably going to be a  really big game changer and definitely  something that will make things like  this not just easier but also going to  make a lot more possible because just by  being able to rotate all of these  different objects into all sorts of  different rotations you can make so many  more uses out of them than they  originally had and it's aside from that  though I think the Alpha 2 is also going  to give a lot of like building  improvements in these smaller pieces  that it's going to add it's going to add  some large oh [ __ ] that was a pan it's  going to add some large improvements in  building pieces but I think the most  important particularly the really small  pieces that the second Alpha will add  like small pillars and small blocks  which will be definitely very versatile  I think in making all sorts of different  things that the original themes of the  game don't have and allow for a lot more  creativity than we already have in the  game so far  so in short and this is something which  I'll get back to you in the next video  because the next video is more or less  going to be a closer of this park but  yeah in short I am really really looking  forward to alpha 2 and I also do have  some pretty big plans I'm just not sure  if I'll really be able to get to them  too soon but yeah I walk out back to  alpha 2 and hopefully it is going to be  really amazing but thank you guys for  watching this episode though I am just  about running out of time lapse at the  moment so I guess I'll see you guys  later  in the next episode though I'll just be  ahead in the time-lapse a little bit  since some of the finishing off will be  done off screen but I'll finish the park  in the next episode so hope to see you  then  you
 

